Modifications
-------------
Two changes, in a commit separate from the unmodified vendoring commit, both
removing a dependency on the rest of the RVC webui (which this project does
not vendor):

1. `tools.cuda_graph.run_cuda_graph` is called at two sites purely to cache
   repeated inference calls via CUDA-graph capture; both are replaced with a
   direct call to the exact function the removed wrapper was passed
   (`self.model(mel)` and `self.mel_extractor(audio, center=center)`
   respectively). This changes nothing about the computation.
2. `RMVPE.__init__`'s device/dtype resolution imported `configs.config`
   (the webui's own infer-device and SM-based half-precision heuristic) to
   resolve an unset device or to override an explicit `cuda` device's
   dtype. This project always passes `device` and `is_half` explicitly from
   `src/vapt/data/rmvpe_infer.py`, so both branches were replaced with that
   explicit choice (an unset device picks cuda-if-available else cpu; an
   explicit device/dtype is used as given, with no SM-based override).

See the `VAPT CHANGE` comments in rmvpe.py at each site.

No other content of this file was modified.
